# 'Insufficient funds' occurrences — grand-e2e runs
# Collected 2026-08-04T15:58:54Z
#
# TWO DISTINCT SOURCES — do not conflate:
#
#   [A] BATCHER  'Insufficient Funds: could not balance dust'  (998 occurrences)
#       The batcher has no spendable dust coin. It then waits 60s, retries a
#       balance it has ALREADY predicted will fail, re-queues, and repeats
#       forever. Product issue: it should skip/park the input and surface the
#       condition instead of consuming a worker slot on a doomed attempt.
#
#   [B] SUITE    'Insufficient funds' from genesis fan-out       (349 occurrences)
#       Self-inflicted by the test's funding: chunk N+1 spends chunk N's
#       change, which does not exist until chunk N confirms. The retry loop
#       absorbs it, so it is benign — but it only exists because the funding
#       plan mints far more coins than a short run needs (432 coins for a
#       25-offer run), forcing ~36 sequential chunks.

